WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.130
Good morning, Hank.

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:04.000
It's Tuesday, and in a stunning turn of events
I find myself... in an airport.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Wardrobe change!

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.721
Hank, today's video comes to you in four very
special parts.

00:00:06.721 --> 00:00:07.721
Part one: your tour!

00:00:07.721 --> 00:00:08.810
Hank, your tour seems to be going well.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:10.260
I wish I was there, but you know what?

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.750
I-I can't sing or play an instrument, so I
would be kind of irrelevant.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.470
Reviews of your tour so far include that it
was "so fun," that people had "the best time

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:22.439
ever," and that you are a "surprisingly competent
musician."

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:24.460
Which analysis I have to say I agree with,
Hank.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.890
I mean back in 2007 when you released your
love song for Helen Hunt, I had no idea that

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:32.730
you could even play the guitar- let alone
write and sing.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.980
And watching that video my main feeling wasn't
like "oh this is a great song" or anything,

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.180
although it was, it was "when did Hank get
a guitar?"

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:41.670
So, yeah, Nerdfighters, if you're in any of
these cities, go to Hank's tour.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:45.050
Part two: Batman's Just a Rich Guy With an
Affinity for Bats.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:48.360
So Hank, when I showed our two competing shirt
designs to Sarah, she laughed for like eight

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.690
minutes and then finally said "Why would anyone
buy a shirt that says 'Batman's just a rich

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.260
guy with an affinity for bats'?"

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:55.260
So, yeah.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.250
If I can't even convert my wife, I'm concerned
about my ability to win this contest.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:02.610
But both these shirts are available for preorder
until April, 25th and then they will never

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.359
be available again....

00:01:04.359 --> 00:01:06.189
I mean unless they are for some reason.

00:01:06.189 --> 00:01:07.189
I don't know.

00:01:07.189 --> 00:01:08.329
The future is unpredictable.

00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:09.789
Part three: Why We're in the Airport.

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:14.260
So, Hank, Sarah and I are on our way to attend
gala (gay-la) or possibly a gala (gah-la).

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:15.260
Hold on....

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.260
According to the dictionary, both are acceptable.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:17.260
It's like GIF and JIFF.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:20.810
So, we're going to a gala (gay-la) gala (gah-la)-
the word so fancy, they named it twice.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:24.250
This gala (gay-la) gala (gah-la) is to celebrate
the Time 100, Time magazine's list of the

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.759
100 most important people in the world.

00:01:25.759 --> 00:01:29.509
Hank, you might remember that ridiculously
last year, I-I was on that list.

00:01:29.509 --> 00:01:33.429
This year I have apparently declined in importance,
so didn't make the list, but I did snag an

00:01:33.429 --> 00:01:34.619
invite to the party!

00:01:34.619 --> 00:01:37.590
I can't tell you how excited I am to have
declined in significance, Hank.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:38.590
Long may it continue.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:42.719
This could save me the embarrassment of having
to explain to other members of the Time 100

00:01:42.719 --> 00:01:45.969
exactly why I was on the list- which happened
a lot at last year's gala (gay-la) gala (gah-la).

00:01:45.969 --> 00:01:49.259
Rand Paul, or whatever, would be like "Who
are you exactly?" and I would be like "Oh,

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:52.859
I'm the guy who popularized the phrase French
the Llama" and he would be like "Yeah, that's

00:01:52.859 --> 00:01:53.859
not a thing."

00:01:53.859 --> 00:01:54.859
This year, I don't have to do any of that
stuff.

00:01:54.859 --> 00:01:57.659
When people ask who I am, I'll just be like
"I'm Rand Paul's date."

00:01:57.659 --> 00:01:59.259
Part four: Strange Marriages

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:03.060
Hank, your airport video about strange marriages
reminded me of a strange marriage I just heard

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.270
about... or at least a strange engagement.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:08.690
So, many years ago, Hank, in 2008 the first
Nerdfighter gathering in Europe that I attended

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.390
happened in Amsterdam.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:13.160
There were like 30 or 40 Nerdfighters there
and it was just kinda like a party!

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:17.500
And after it had been going on for about an
hour a Dutch Nerdfighter I knew from her video

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.190
series, "Best Wishes from The Netherlands",
came up to me and she was like: "Can you introduce

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:23.420
us to the Belgian boys they have cute accents?"

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:31.140
And now 7 years later one of those Dutch girls-
now woman- is marrying one of those Belgian

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:32.330
boys-now man!

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.670
So congratulations to them...

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:36.040
I love it when Nerdfighter-like turns into
Nerdfighter-love.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.280
So Hank the weirdest part is that at any one
of your concerts in the next couple of weeks

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.010
like Nerdfighters could meet and fall in love
and 7 years later get engaged!

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.910
Okay they just called my name for final boarding
call, I, uhh, oh boy.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:50.840
I've got like, my tux shoes and my backpack
and everything is totally disorganized.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:54.190
I hope I make it to the plane, I hope I make
it to the plane.....

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.190
MADE IT.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:55.820
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

